1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:06,981
Safe inside Curio, Noah and Mila watch the storm.

2
00:00:07,031 --> 00:00:07,793
Lightning!

3
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:09,092
One, two, three…

4
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:09,498
BOOM!

5
00:00:09,548 --> 00:00:12,308
Why does the thunder come so late?

6
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,403
Mila counts every time.

7
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:16,730
Sometimes three seconds, sometimes ten!

8
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:19,227
As if the noise were dawdling on the way…

9
00:00:20,022 --> 00:00:21,536
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:24,604
Mini mode!

11
00:00:24,654 --> 00:00:27,845
Lightning is burning hot: it heats the air all at once,

12
00:00:27,895 --> 00:00:29,023
hotter than the Sun!

13
00:00:29,073 --> 00:00:31,262
The air swells so fast that it cracks:

14
00:00:31,312 --> 00:00:32,196
that's thunder.

15
00:00:32,971 --> 00:00:34,248
They leave together.

16
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:37,100
But the light zooms: it arrives right away.

17
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:39,024
Sound moves much more slowly,

18
00:00:39,074 --> 00:00:42,324
three hundred meters per second: it arrives late!

19
00:00:43,121 --> 00:00:43,655
So count!

20
00:00:43,705 --> 00:00:47,027
Three seconds between the lightning and the thunder:

21
00:00:47,077 --> 00:00:49,102
the storm is one kilometer away.

22
00:00:49,152 --> 00:00:50,967
Six seconds: two kilometers.

23
00:00:51,758 --> 00:00:53,485
Noah counts: fifteen seconds.

24
00:00:53,535 --> 00:00:56,611
The storm is five kilometers away, it's moving off.

25
00:00:56,661 --> 00:00:58,511
But as long as we hear thunder,

26
00:00:58,561 --> 00:00:59,481
we stay inside!

27
00:01:00,264 --> 00:01:02,892
That's why thunder comes after lightning.

28
00:01:03,805 --> 00:01:06,570
The light of the lightning arrives right away;

29
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,191
the sound of thunder takes time to travel.

30
00:01:09,951 --> 00:01:11,493
With an adult, behind the window:

31
00:01:11,543 --> 00:01:14,002
when you see the lightning, count until the thunder.

32
00:01:14,052 --> 00:01:15,352
Three seconds per kilometer:

33
00:01:15,402 --> 00:01:16,753
you know where the storm is!

34
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:20,227
And how does a magnet attract metal?

35
00:01:20,277 --> 00:01:21,570
The answer tomorrow.
